      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the number of books left over after repacking, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of books in the warehouse.\n2. Determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made from the total number of books.\n3. Calculate the number of books left over after making as many full boxes as possible.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of books in the warehouse. There are 1335 boxes, and each box contains 39 books. Therefore, the total number of books is:\n\\[\n1335 \\times 39\n\\]\nWe can break this multiplication down for easier calculation:\n\\[\n1335 \\times 39 = 1335 \\times (40 - 1) = 1335 \\times 40 - 1335 \\times 1 = 53400 - 1335 = 52065\n\\]\nSo, there are 52065 books in total.\n\nNext, we need to determine how many full boxes of 40 books can be made from 52065 books. We do this by dividing 52065 by 40:\n\\[\n52065 \\div 40 = 1301 \\text{ R } 25\n\\]\nThis means that 52065 divided by 40 gives a quotient of 1301 and a remainder of 25. The quotient 1301 tells us that we can make 1301 full boxes of 40 books each. The remainder 25 tells us that after making these 1301 boxes, we will have 25 books left over.\n\nTherefore, the number of books left over is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]",
