      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine how many books Melvin will have left over after repacking them into boxes with 40 books each, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total number of books:**\n   Each box contains 39 books, and there are 1335 boxes.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of books} = 1335 \\times 39\n   \\]\n\n2. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 39 = 1335 \\times (40 - 1) = 1335 \\times 40 - 1335 \\times 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 40 = 53400\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1335 \\times 1 = 1335\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total number of books} = 53400 - 1335 = 52065\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the number of books per new box and the remainder:**\n   Each new box will contain 40 books. To find out how many full boxes of 40 books can be made and how many books are left over, we perform the division:\n   \\[\n   52065 \\div 40\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   52065 \\div 40 = 1301 \\text{ R } 25\n   \\]\n   Here, 1301 is the number of full boxes, and 25 is the remainder.\n\nTherefore, after repacking the books into boxes with 40 books each, Melvin will have \\(\\boxed{25}\\) books left over.",
